// Destinations for `transcript_probe`, with the ways a transcript of each
// one can come out wrong.
//
// READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING A NUMBER FROM IT.
//
// The `heard` entries below are SEEDED BY HAND — plausible confusions,
// not recordings. Exactly one of them is observed fact: "Jalebi" for
// Jollibee, which `config.WHISPER_INITIAL_PROMPTS` exists to correct.
// The rest are guesses at what a decoder might do, and a guess scored to
// one decimal place is still a guess.
//
// Replace them with real transcripts as you collect them. `heard` is a
// list precisely so a real one can be appended next to the invented one
// and the two compared. The honest way to fill it: record yourself
// saying each destination on the Pi, run Whisper over the clips, and
// paste what comes out — mistakes included, verbatim, with no tidying.
//
// What a misheard place name actually looks like
// ----------------------------------------------
//
// Whisper has no character-level fallback. It cannot spell a word it was
// never trained on, so an out-of-vocabulary name is not emitted as a
// near-miss spelling — it is emitted as whatever sequence of words the
// decoder DOES know that best fits the audio. The error types below are
// in rough order of how much damage they do to `name_match_score`, which
// compares whole tokens:
//
//   substitution   the name becomes a different real word
//                  Bulacnin -> "Bull Acne", Marawoy -> "Marrow Way"
//   boundary       one word is split, or two are joined
//                  Inosloban -> "In Oslo Ban", Lipa City Hall -> "Lipa Cityhall"
//   initials       an initialled street has no stable spoken form at all
//                  B. Morada -> "Be Morada" / "Bee Morada" / "B Morada"
//   spelling       a near-miss on a name the decoder half-knows
//                  Jollibee -> "Jollybee"
//
// Only the last one is the ordinary idea of a typo, and it is the least
// of the four. A substitution shares NO tokens with the true name, so
// the name signal does not degrade — it disappears, every candidate ties
// at 0.00, and ranking silently becomes a pure distance sort. That is
// the mechanism this probe is pointed at.
//
// Fields
//   group    chain | local | street | barangay | category — reported
//            separately, ordered by how much of the name Whisper's
//            vocabulary already holds
//   place    the canonical spelling. Also the CONTROL: the probe always
//            tests this string too, and the gap between it and `heard` is
//            the whole measurement. Do NOT repeat it inside `heard` —
//            the loader rejects that, because it counts the control twice
//   origin   "lat,lon" the user is standing at
//   nearest  mirrors the NLU's `nearest` parameter — ranking ignores the
//            name entirely when true
//   heard    misheard forms only
//   truth    OPTIONAL "lat,lon". Only needed when geocoding `place`
//            itself lands somewhere wrong — see the probe's docstring
//
// Origins are in Lipa City, Batangas, the same fix used throughout the
// repo's routing tests. These places must exist in YOUR Photon extract:
// a case whose control fails is reported as unusable and not scored, so
// a wrong guess here costs a line of output, not a wrong result.

// --- national chains -------------------------------------------------------
// In Whisper's vocabulary, and `WHISPER_INITIAL_PROMPTS` backstops the
// `tiny` English model where it is not. The easy tier, and the one that
// says whether anything is wrong upstream of spelling. Errors here are
// mild: spelling and boundary, rarely substitution.
{"group":"chain","place":"Jollibee","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":true,"heard":["Jalebi","Jolly Bee","Jollybee","Jelly Bee"]}
{"group":"chain","place":"Mang Inasal","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":true,"heard":["Mang in a sal","Mongin Asal","Man Enistle","Mangin Hassle"]}
{"group":"chain","place":"Chowking","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":true,"heard":["Chow King","Chalking","Shaolin King"]}
{"group":"chain","place":"Mercury Drug","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":true,"heard":["Mercury Drugs","Mercury Drag","Mercurio Drug"]}
{"group":"chain","place":"7-Eleven","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":true,"heard":["Seven Eleven","711","Seven Levin"]}
{"group":"chain","place":"SM City Lipa","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["SM Lipa","Essem Lipa","SM Leper","Asem Lipa"]}
{"group":"chain","place":"Puregold","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":true,"heard":["Pure Gold","Pure Goal","Pyur Gold"]}

// --- named local landmarks -------------------------------------------------
// Mostly English and Spanish words the decoder knows, assembled into a
// name it does not. Expect boundary errors and the odd substitution on
// the one Tagalog or Spanish token.
{"group":"local","place":"Lipa City Hall","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["Lipa Cityhall","Leper City Hall","Lipa City Hole","Lee Pa City Hall"]}
{"group":"local","place":"San Sebastian Cathedral","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["Sansebastian Cathedral","San Sebastien Cathedral","Sun Sebastian Cathedral"]}
{"group":"local","place":"Batangas State University","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["Batanga State University","Bat Angus State University","Batangas State Universe","Batangas Estate University"]}
{"group":"local","place":"Lipa City Public Market","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["Lipa Public Market","Leepa City Public Market","Lipa City Palengke","Lee Park City Public Market"]}

// --- streets ---------------------------------------------------------------
// Filipino street names are overwhelmingly initialled surnames, and an
// initial has no stable spoken form: "B." is said "bee" and written "B",
// "B.", "Be" or "Bee" depending on nothing the device controls. The
// surname behind it is usually out of vocabulary as well, so these carry
// two independent errors in one short name.
{"group":"street","place":"B. Morada Avenue","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["Be Morada Avenue","Bee Morada Avenue","B Morada Ave","Be More Rada Avenue"]}
{"group":"street","place":"P. Torres Street","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["P Torres Street","Pee Torres Street","Petorres Street","Pea Taurus Street"]}
{"group":"street","place":"C.M. Recto Avenue","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["CM Recto Avenue","See Em Recto Avenue","CM Rector Avenue","Seam Wrecked Oh Avenue"]}
{"group":"street","place":"J.P. Laurel Highway","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["JP Laurel Highway","Jay Pee Laurel Highway","Jaypee Lorel Highway","J P Laural Highway"]}
{"group":"street","place":"Gen. Luna Street","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["Gen Luna Street","Jen Luna Street","General Una Street","Gentle Una Street"]}

// --- barangays -------------------------------------------------------------
// The hard tier, and the reason this probe exists. Tagalog toponyms are
// out of vocabulary for an English model and thin even in the Tagalog
// one, so the decoder reaches for English words that sound similar. The
// results share no tokens at all with the true name — which is precisely
// the case `name_match_score` scores at 0.00.
{"group":"barangay","place":"Bulacnin","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["Bull Acnin","Bull Acne","Boolak Nin","Bulaknin"]}
{"group":"barangay","place":"Marawoy","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["Mara Woy","Marrow Way","Mar Away","Maraguay"]}
{"group":"barangay","place":"Inosloban","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["In Oslo Ban","Inos Loban","Enos Loban","Enoch Sloban"]}
{"group":"barangay","place":"Sabang","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["Sabong","Saw Bang","Sa Bang","Suh Bong"]}
{"group":"barangay","place":"Bugtong na Pulo","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["Bug Tong Na Pulo","Bugtong Napulo","Book Tong Na Pulo","Bug Tongue Na Polo"]}
{"group":"barangay","place":"Mataas na Lupa","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["Matas Na Lupa","Mataas Nalupa","Mata As Na Lupa","My Toss Na Lupa"]}
{"group":"barangay","place":"Pinagtongulan","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["Pinag Tongulan","Pina Tongulan","Pinang Tongulan","Peenag Tongue Yulan"]}
{"group":"barangay","place":"Tangob","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":false,"heard":["Tango B","Tangub","Tan Gob","Tango Bee"]}

// --- category queries ------------------------------------------------------
// The control group, and expected to be immune: these are ordinary words
// the decoder gets right, and `rank_candidates` ignores the name entirely
// when `nearest` is true. If this tier degrades, the problem is not
// spelling and the rest of the probe is measuring the wrong thing.
{"group":"category","place":"hospital","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":true,"heard":["ospital","hospitals"]}
{"group":"category","place":"pharmacy","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":true,"heard":["parmacy","botika"]}
{"group":"category","place":"church","origin":"13.937387,121.118698","nearest":true,"heard":["simbahan","churches"]}
